# design-system.mdc
## Pathways Within Design System & Component Standards

> **IMPORTANT:** This file contains specifications (the *what*).
> For design judgment and aesthetic principles (the *how* and *why*), 
> see `cursor-constitution/rules/design-philosophy.mdc`.
> The philosophy file MUST be read before implementing any design.

### DESIGN SOURCE
- Brand Guidelines: Pathways_Within_Style_Guide.pdf
- Logo: Circular labyrinth/maze motif with "Wisdom and Wellness Collaborative" tagline
- Style: Calming, clean lines, not complicated or overly busy

### INDUSTRY CONTEXT
**Industry:** Healthcare/Mental Health + Holistic Wellness (NOT "spa" or "medspa")
**Design Philosophy:** 
- **UNIFIED 360° approach** — Services are integrated, NOT presented side by side
- Labyrinth metaphor: One entry, many personalized routes
- Trauma informed design (no aggressive urgency, no time pressure)
- Calm, easy navigation (reduce cognitive load)
- Clear visual hierarchy
- Progressive disclosure (don't overwhelm)
- Mobile first responsive
- Reduced motion as DEFAULT for mental health contexts

**Critical Design Note:** The visual design should reflect the labyrinth logo — whatever path you choose, you receive a personalized journey. Do NOT design two separate columns or "choose your path" layouts. Services flow together as one collaborative care environment.

